          },
          {
            "id": 1809,
            "sort": 2,
            "name": "Overview",
            "value": "<p>Overall, the proposed plan shows significant urban development with major infrastructure changes and an enhanced transportation network. The most notable transformation involves replacing the airfield with an industrial estate and implementing a new road system.</p>",
            "question_id": 18359,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 1810,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<p>Starting from the top, the most significant change involves the complete removal of the airfield, which will be replaced by a large industrial estate in the northern area. This new industrial estate will be connected to the railway system, and the railway line will be extended northward to serve the development. Moving toward the center, an additional roundabout will be constructed on the northern side of the gas station, positioned between the existing roundabout on the A2 route and the Town Center. The gas station will remain unchanged in its current western location.</p>",
            "question_id": 18359,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 1811,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<p>Regarding transportation infrastructure, the current build-up area ring road around the town center will be partially removed, with only the northern section retained, while a new road will be constructed outside the town center. Additionally, a new ring road called A4 will be built on the southern side, creating connections between the A2 route, the railway line, and the southern part of the town center. This A4 road will run parallel to the current central route, providing an alternative transportation corridor.</p>",
